"**Eligible Patients**" means patients registered at the Surgery who are resident in the Wrenfield Council area;

"**Funding Period**" means the period from 1 April 2023 to 31 March 2024 inclusive;

"**Parties**" means the Trust, the Council and the Surgery, and "Party" means any one of them;

"**Project**" means the community health outreach programme described in Schedule 1;

"**Service Users**" means persons who receive services under this Agreement.

2.2 The headings in this Agreement are for convenience only and shall not affect its interpretation.

---

**3. PURPOSE AND OBJECTIVES**

3.1 The purpose of this Agreement is to deliver a coordinated programme of community health outreach in the Greenfield ward, with the objective of:

(a) reducing avoidable hospital admissions among the elderly and housebound population;

(b) improving early detection of long-term conditions, particularly type 2 diabetes and hypertension;

(c) increasing uptake of flu and COVID-19 vaccinations among eligible residents;

(d) providing social prescribing referrals to address non-clinical factors affecting health.

3.2 The parties acknowledge that the objectives set out in Clause 3.1 are shared objectives and agree to work together in a spirit of cooperation and mutual respect.

---

**4. FUNDING AND FINANCIAL PROVISIONS**

4.1 The Council agrees to provide funding to the Trust for the purposes of delivering the Project in accordance with this Agreement.

4.2 The total grant funding for the Funding Period shall be **£15,000 (fifteen thousand pounds)** .

4.3 The grant funding shall be paid by the Council to the Trust in two instalments, as follows:

