(a) the first instalment of £10,000 shall be paid within 30 days of the date of this Agreement;

(b) the second instalment of £5,000 shall be paid upon receipt by the Council of the interim report referred to in Clause 7.2, provided that such report is received by 31 December 2023.

4.4 The Trust shall hold the grant funding in a separate designated account and shall ensure that all expenditure is properly recorded and attributable to the Project.

4.5 The grant funding may only be used for the purposes set out in Schedule 1 and in accordance with the budget breakdown set out in Schedule 3.

4.6 Any unspent grant funding at the end of the Funding Period shall be returned to the Council within 60 days of the end of the Funding Period, unless the parties agree in writing to carry forward such unspent funds to the following financial year.

4.7 The Trust shall not use the grant funding for any purpose other than the Project without the prior written consent of the Council.

4.8 The Trust shall ensure that the grant funding is not used to subsidise or cross-subsidise any other activity, including the routine provision of GP services.

---

**5. ROLES AND RESPONSIBILITIES OF THE PARTIES**

5.1 **The Trust shall:**

(a) act as the accountable body for the grant funding;

(b) employ or contract with the project coordinator and community health workers required to deliver the Project;

(c) provide clinical supervision for the community health workers;

(d) maintain appropriate records of all activities and expenditure;

(e) submit reports to the Council in accordance with Clause 7;

(f) ensure that all staff involved in the Project have appropriate Disclosure and Barring Service checks where required.

5.2 **The Council shall:**

(a) provide the grant funding in accordance with Clause 4;

(b) provide data and intelligence relating to the health needs of the Greenfield ward population, subject to data protection requirements;

**PARTNERSHIP AGREEMENT – GREENFIELD SURGERY**

**RENEWAL AND AMENDMENT AGREEMENT NO. 2**

**Parties:**

(1) West Cumbria Health Trust, a body established pursuant to the National Health Service Act 2006, whose principal office is at The Old Mill, Mill Lane, Cleator Moor, Cumbria, CA25 5QH (the "Trust");

(2) Greenfield Surgery, a GP practice operating from Greenfield Health Centre, 14 Station Road, Egremont, Cumbria, CA22 2RP (the "Practice").

**Background**

This Agreement is a further renewal and amendment of the Partnership Agreement dated 12 January 2023 between the Trust and the Practice, as previously amended by a Renewal and Amendment Agreement dated 31 March 2024 (together, the "Original Agreement").

**1. DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION**

1.1 In this Agreement, unless the context otherwise requires:

"Agreement" means this Renewal and Amendment Agreement No. 2 together with the Original Agreement as amended by it;

"Effective Date" means 1 April 2025;

"Review Date" means 31 March 2026;

"Project" means the Greenfield Community Health Outreach Project;

"Parties" means the Trust and the Practice;

"Service Year" means the period from 1 April in any year to 31 March in the following year.

1.2 Clause headings are for convenience only and shall not affect interpretation.

1.3 References to clauses and Schedules are to clauses of and Schedules to this Agreement unless otherwise stated.

**2. RENEWAL**

2.1 The Original Agreement, as amended by this Agreement, is renewed with effect from the Effective Date and expiring on the Review Date.

2.2 The Parties shall review the operation of the Agreement on or before the Review Date and may agree to a further renewal in writing.

2.3 Termination provisions in clause 11 of the Original Agreement shall continue to apply, provided that any notice served after the Effective Date shall take effect no later than the Review Date unless the Parties otherwise agree in writing.

**3. AMENDMENTS TO SERVICES**

3.1 Schedule 1 of the Original Agreement is amended by replacing the description of the outreach service with the description set out in Schedule 1 of this Agreement. The principal changes are:

(a) the addition of a weekly wellbeing drop-in session at the Community Hall, Main Street, Egremont, to commence no later than 1 June 2024;

(b) the removal of the term-time school-based healthy eating workshops, which were discontinued by mutual consent in November 2023;

(c) an increase in the target number of home visits for housebound patients from 12 to 15 per month, reflecting demand identified during the first year of the Project.

3.2 For the avoidance of doubt, all other services described in Schedule 1 of the Original Agreement remain unchanged.

**4. AMENDMENTS TO PERFORMANCE INDICATORS**

4.1 Schedule 2 of the Original Agreement is amended as follows:

(a) Indicator 4 (number of patients referred to the Practice's social prescriber) is revised from "at least 8 per quarter" to "at least 10 per quarter";

(b) Indicator 7 (patient satisfaction score) is revised from "at least 85%" to "at least 88%";

(c) a new Indicator 10 is added: "at least 20 attendees per month at the weekly wellbeing drop-in session, averaged over each quarter";

(d) the baseline data for Indicator 4 is updated to reflect actual performance in the year ending 31 March 2024.

**5. AMENDMENTS TO FUNDING AND BUDGET**

5.1 The budget set out in Schedule 3 of the Original Agreement is replaced by the budget set out in Schedule 3 of this Agreement.

5.2 The Trust shall pay the Practice the sum set out in Schedule 3 in twelve equal monthly instalments, payable in arrears within 30 days of receipt of a valid invoice.
